    },
    {
      "id": "fan-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 210,
      "y": 534,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "text": "Fan is UPSTREAM of the ARM switch — a parallel tap, not in series — so it runs whenever the 12 V branch is live.\nDownstream it would stop the instant the operator disarms a diode that was dissipating 2.5 W.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.476Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.476Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "tap-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 434,
      "y": 506,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "text": "The GPIO 24 sense tap is downstream of both (drawing 3), so an open door reads as a disarm.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.476Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.476Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
