    },
    {
      "id": "par-lbl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 712,
      "y": 742,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "text": "in parallel",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.477Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.477Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "coil-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 798,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "text": "Tapped UPSTREAM of K1's own\nmain poles — otherwise the coil\ncould never pull in.",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.477Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.477Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "seal-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 952,
      "y": 798,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "text": "START energises the coil; the auxiliary contact then closes and holds it.\nAnything that breaks the series path drops K1, which opens the auxiliary\ncontact and destroys the hold. Nothing re-energises K1 but another START.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.477Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.477Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "bhead",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 912,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "text": "BEHAVIOUR",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.477Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.477Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "btable",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 940,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "text": "EVENT                            K1                    ±15 V and 12 V     TO RESTORE\nMains applied at the isolator    de-energised          OFF                press START\nSTART pressed, then released     energised, sealed in  ON                 —\nE-STOP pressed                   drops out             OFF                release E-stop, THEN press START\nE-STOP released                  stays de-energised    OFF                press START\nEnclosure door opened            drops out             OFF                close door, THEN press START\nMains dip or interruption        drops out             OFF                press START",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.477Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.477Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "key1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 1086,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "text": "Releasing the mushroom restores nothing. Only a deliberate START press does — that is the whole point of the seal-in circuit.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.477Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.477Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "key2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 1110,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "text": "The Pi is NOT on K1. It keeps running on its own USB-C supply, so the log, the GPIO 25 sense circuit and the 5 V logic rail holding the laser-path pull-downs all survive an E-stop.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.478Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.478Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "key3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 1134,
      "strokeColor": "#e8590c",
      "text": "Residual risk: a welded K1 main pole means the coil drops and the supplies stay live. Detecting that needs a monitored safety relay with mirror-contact feedback (IEC 60947-4-1) — an open item.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.478Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T09:57:49.478Z",
      "version": 1
    },
